        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T12:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If by collision, you mean ensuring 2 different app owners do not have the same instance-id, I think that would require checking a central db for all existing entries and I\u0027m actually not sure we need need to do that?\n\nFor randomly picked instance-id, we can rely on randomness across large size (previously 64 bytes \u0026 now 60) to ensure no collision.\nFor others, if we can ensure the instance-id are in correct range, we can trust the client to pick a unique instance-id?\n\nAlthough I do like the idea of continuing the bookkeeping of these caller claimed static `instance-Id`. Perhaps the caller(libavf) calls `IVirtualizationService::claimVmInstance`?  This will record the instance-id in a central db for maintenance purposes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "f20605ab620509b25545d2f1640e9a041c421f36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc5facce_b19bb40e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T00:02:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think that would require checking a central db for all existing entries and I\u0027m actually not sure we need need to do that?\n\nMaybe it is OK to not validate it via a cental DB, I\u0027m just saying we that we haven\u0027t agreed on what the solution is.\n\n\u003e For others, if we can ensure the instance-id are in correct range, we can trust the client to pick a unique instance-id?\n\nEnsuring that is the tricky part. This CL only ensures it for vendor callers.",
      "parentUuid": "9b289e4d_1e8e2168",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "f20605ab620509b25545d2f1640e9a041c421f36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e80a29ad_b22acb5f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T11:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Ensuring that is the tricky part. This CL only ensures it for vendor callers\n\nHow about having the caller ensure that. For vendor callers, if libavf is the only entry point, perhaps we can introduce the check here[1].\n\nFor system callers, I would think the situation is trickier with the lack of uniform entrypoint(they can use RawConfig). \n\n[1] https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/libavf/src/lib.rs;l\u003d102",
      "parentUuid": "cc5facce_b19bb40e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "f20605ab620509b25545d2f1640e9a041c421f36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10102183_d78b6ee6",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
