      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T09:16:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`allocateInstanceId` is [invoked](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/framework-virtualization/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java;l\u003d551;drc\u003dcf9784a5605096c247eb8206061d755bc302a41d) by the underlying Java API during VM creation. Specifically, when a VM is created like [this](http://google3/java/com/google/android/libraries/abuse/hades/moirai/pvm/LocalVirtualMachineInitializer.kt;l\u003d43;rcl\u003d611251547), the VM config builder [sets up](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/framework-virtualization/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java;l\u003d441;drc\u003da60b8c1f6f5539de4c8f464c1eaa11242ffb8729) a file path for the instance ID. Subsequently, `allocateInstanceId` is invoked to populate this file with a randomly generated ID.\n\nGiven that these VMs (e.g., [TARTARUS_VM](//java/com/google/android/libraries/abuse/hades/moirai/pvm:virtual_machine_initializer)) are created via the system API, I\u0027m not sure they were placed in the vendor partition, thus I\u0027m concerned that this validation check might inadvertently prevent them from running. wdyt?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 616,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 616,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "f20605ab620509b25545d2f1640e9a041c421f36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
