        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T12:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIU, you are suggesting: \n\n1) AVF reserved range (allocation is random atm) - Proposed to start with 0x77777777, irrespective of the caller (vendor/system).\n2) Reserved for static instance-id owned by vendor like partititon - Proposed to start with 0xFFFFFFFF\n3) [By extension] Reserved for static instance-id owned by system like partititon- Start with 0x00000000\n4) Rest reserved for unspecified purposed which can be used in future.\n\nIf so, LGTM at this patch set.\n\nThere is another set of id (payload-id) derived currently from instance-id used to acces Secretkeeper for entries in Microdroid. We need to account for these in terms of collision \u0026 I\u0027m wondering if we can use 4. Shifting the discussion to b/364629416 as that is out of scope of this patch",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 466,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 466,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "f20605ab620509b25545d2f1640e9a041c421f36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af6b25dd_a9608199",
        "filename": "android/virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 466,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T00:02:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but I\u0027m only suggesting (1) and (2) in this CL.\n\n\u003e 1) AVF reserved range (allocation is random atm) - Proposed to start with 0x77777777, irrespective of the caller (vendor/system).\n\nThis code isn\u0027t accessible by vendor yet (they *have* to use static IDs), so we could decide to use a different prefix for allocated vendor IDs later.\n\n\u003e 3) [By extension] Reserved for static instance-id owned by system like partititon- Start with 0x00000000\n\nThat\u0027s OK with me, but it might be smart to avoid all zeros.",
      "parentUuid": "dd171c5e_be396f0d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 466,
        "startChar": 8,
